{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1069", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Dear Team\n\nI hope this message finds you well and thriving in your daily endeavors. I am reaching out to formally invite you to an important gathering that will take place next week and is designed to bring together key contributors who are deeply invested in the evolution of our current initiatives. This meeting is not just another routine check in but a strategic moment for us to align our efforts and share insights that are truly correlated with the outcomes we are striving to achieve.\n\nOver the past few months we have seen remarkable progress across multiple departments and your individual contributions have played a vital role in this momentum. Many of you are currently experiencing new challenges and opportunities that demand thoughtful dialogue and collaborative problem solving. This meeting is intended to create a space where those experiences can be openly shared without judgment and where we can collectively identify patterns and strategies that will guide us forward.\n\nThe session will be held on Tuesday June 18th at 1000 AM in the main conference room on the fifth floor. We have reserved the room for three hours to allow ample time for discussion reflection and planning. If you are unable to attend in person please know that a live virtual link will be provided so that you can join remotely without disruption to your schedule. We strongly encourage everyone to participate whether in person or online because your voice matters and your perspective is essential.\n\nWe will begin the meeting with a brief overview of our current objectives followed by a series of short presentations from team leads who have been working closely on projects that are directly correlated with our long term goals. After these presentations we will open the floor for group discussion. We want to hear what you are experiencing on the front lines what barriers you have encountered and what solutions you believe could make the biggest impact. This is not a top down directive session but a co creation space where all ideas are welcomed and valued.\n\nWe have also prepared a short survey that will be sent to you by the end of this week. Please take a few minutes to complete it before the meeting. Your responses will help us tailor the agenda to address the most pressing concerns and to ensure that the time we spend together is as productive and meaningful as possible. The survey is anonymous and will only be used to guide our conversation.\n\nLight refreshments will be provided during the break and we will conclude the session with a collaborative action plan that outlines next steps and assigns clear responsibilities. We believe that when people feel heard and included they are more likely to take ownership of the outcomes. That is why we are making this meeting a priority.\n\nPlease confirm your attendance by Friday June 14th so we can finalize seating arrangements and materials. If you have any special accessibility needs or require additional accommodations please let us know immediately so we can make the necessary arrangements.\n\nThank you for your continued dedication and for being part of a team that is not just working hard but thinking deeply and acting with purpose. We are excited to learn from you and to build something extraordinary together.\n\nWarm regards\n\nThe Planning Committee", "logprobs": [{"token": "Dear", "logprob": -0.038177624344825745}, {"token": " Team", "logprob": -0.2163379192352295}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.058827295899391174}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -0.01372460275888443}, {"token": " hope", "logprob": -0.011072618886828423}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -8.570780482841656e-05}, {"token": " message", "logprob": -2.407998726994265e-05}, {"token": " finds", "logprob": -1.1086402082582936e-05}, {"token": " you", "logprob": -0.0008550802012905478}, {"token": " well", "logprob": -0.